From, $p \cdot \tan x=q \cdot \tan y\begin{aligned}
& p^2 \cdot \tan ^2 x=q^2 \cdot \tan ^2 y \\
& \Rightarrow \frac{p^2}{q^2}=\frac{\tan ^2 y}{\tan ^2 x}=\frac{(d-a)}{(b-d)} \cdot \frac{(a-c)}{(c-b)} \\
& \quad=\frac{(a-d)(c-a)}{(b-c)(d-b)}
\end{aligned}$

From $b \sin ^2 y+a \cos ^2 y=d\begin{aligned}
& b \sin ^2 y+a \cos ^2 y=d\left(\sin ^2 y+\cos ^2 y\right) \\
& (b-d) \sin ^2 y=(d-a) \cos ^2 y \\
& \Rightarrow \frac{\sin ^2 y}{\cos ^2 y}=\frac{(d-a)}{(b-d)} \Rightarrow \tan ^2 y=\frac{(d-a)}{(b-d)}
\end{aligned}$
